    "packName": "Boltgun",
    "packDescription": "A .75 calibre war-rifle, hand-forged and rite-blessed in an age that worshipped war, and far too heavy for an ordinary soldier. It does not fire bullets. Each bolt is a small rocket: a powder charge throws it from the barrel, a solid-fuel motor lights a heartbeat later and drives it to 975 m/s, a hardened tip punches through plate, and a mass-reactive fuse waits until the bolt is buried in its target before the charge inside goes off. The thunder of its firing is said to be a prayer, and every kill an answered one.",
